pe filter to correctly include all car components like the Halo Hoop, ensuring proper material assignment by incorporating curve objects. The problematic filter logic, which excludes curve objects, is the root cause of the lighting inconsistencies, and must be corrected. The `v5_anim.py` script's car collection filter must also be updated to ensure all car objects are included, regardless of parent object or name prefix. The fill light energy levels will be tuned through test renders, evaluating pixel brightness and histograms to balance the car body's appearance with the decals, based on preview PNG files.\n\n\nThe analysis of the camera positions reveals a significant issue: the lead distance calculation places the `Cam_S20_StoweTele` camera far outside the track boundary at Stowe corner. This is due to the camera's tangent projection placing it through the barriers and ad boards. The camera's perspective is looking back at the car instead of towards the track.\n\n\nThe initial camera checks identified `Cam_S20_StoweTele` as incorrectly positioned. Now examining `Cam_S03_ChaseRise`, it's potentially blocked by `V5_HedgeRing`; a radius check for the hedge and raycast assessment will determine obstruction and correct coordinate issues. `Cam_S04_Hairpin` has a brake board obstruction (`V5_Brake_1_150`). The visual confirmation in the contact sheet will inform the position fix.\n\n\nAdjusting `Cam_S04_Hairpin` by a small offset completely resolves the brake board obstruction. Now assessing `Cam_S14_HeliDrop`, the camera is briefly blocked by the bridge deck; adjusting its position to eliminate all occlusions across all frames is the target. Examining `Cam_S17_Maggotts`, a barrier blocks the view at the start of the shot; raising the height parameter should fix the occlusion.\n\n\nThe raycast failed to detect the barrier obstruction in `Cam_S20_StoweTele` because the ray hit `V5_Ad_72` first, which was closer to the camera and completely blocked the car at frame `f=1730`. Examination of the contact sheet confirms `V5_Ad_72` (a large yellow rectangle) and the obscured car. The second inspection script will check the local bounding boxes and positions of steering wheel components.\n\n\nThe steering wheel's rotation is controlled by both a driver and a constraint, raising questions about conflicting transformations. The `V4_LimitRot` constraint could be overriding the driver's input, or the steering wheel's mesh might be incorrectly parented to the wrong bone within the armature. Investigating the bone hierarchy and vertex group assignments of the steering wheel mesh is necessary to understand how its position is determined and how to resolve visibility discrepancies in specific camera shots.\n\n\nThe investigation now targets the parenting of various steering wheel and car components, identifying potential issues within the object hierarchy. The shared material `Mat_Neon_Orange` is assigned to both the exhaust inner glow and the FIA rain light; this shared material assignment in the script causes the FIA rain light to be orange instead of red. This material is linked to the rain light object, so the material assignment must be re-evaluated to prevent the unwanted color.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\nimport bpy\nfrom mathutils import Vector\n\nrig = bpy.data.objects[\"RIG_F1_Race\"]\nscene = bpy.context.scene\nscene.frame_set(1)\ndeps = bpy.context.evaluated_depsgraph_get()\n\nprint(\"=== STEERING & COCKPIT OBJECTS ===\")\ntarget_prefixes = (\"GEO_F1_Cockpit\", \"GEO_F1_Steering\", \"GEO_F1_ShiftLED\", \"GEO_F1_Halo\",\n                   \"GEO_F1_Overhead_TCam\", \"GEO_F1_FIA_RainLight\", \"GEO_F1_Exhaust\",\n                   \"GEO_F1_Brake\")\nfor o in sorted(bpy.data.objects, key=lambda x: x.name):\n    if o.name.startswith(target_prefixes):\n        vgs = [vg.name for vg in o.vertex_groups] if hasattr(o, \"vertex_groups\") else []\n        mods = [(m.name, m.type, getattr(m, \"object\", None)) for m in o.modifiers]\n        bb = [o.matrix_world @ Vector(c) for c in o.bound_box]\n        mn = tuple(round(min(v[i] for v in bb), 3) for i in range(3))\n        mx = tuple(round(max(v[i] for v in bb), 3) for i in range(3))\n        print(f\"  {o.name:32s} parent_type={o.parent_type:8s} parent_bone={o.parent_bone!r:20s} vgs={vgs} mods={[(a,b) for a,b,_ in mods]} loc={tuple(round(x,3) for x in o.location)} bbox_local_approx=({mn}..{mx})\")\n\nprint(\"\\n=== BONE CONSTRAINTS DETAIL ===\")\nfor pb in rig.pose.bones:\n    for c in pb.constraints:\n        info = {k: getattr(c, k) for k in dir(c) if k.startswith((\"use_\", \"min_\", \"max_\", \"owner_space\", \"target_space\"))}\n        print(f\"  {pb.name}.{c.name} ({c.type}): {info}\")\n\nprint(\"\\n=== RIG DRIVERS DETAIL ===\")\nif rig.animation_data:\n    for d in rig.animation_data.drivers:\n        vars_info = [(v.name, v.type, [(t.id.name if t.id else None, t.data_path) for t in v.targets]) for v in d.driver.variables]\n        print(f\"  {d.data_path}[{d.array_index}] expr={d.driver.expression!r} vars={vars_info}\")\n\nprint(\"\\n=== MAT_BRAKE_HEATGLOW & MAT_NEON_ORANGE DETAIL ===\")\nfor mname in (\"Mat_Brake_HeatGlow\", \"Mat_BrakeDisc_CarbonCeramic\", \"Mat_Caliper_Anodized\", \"Mat_Neon_Orange\", \"Mat_Steering_LCD_Telemetry\"):\n    m = bpy.data.materials.get(mname)\n    if not m:\n        continue\n    print(f\"Material: {m.name} (users={m.users})\")\n    if m.node_tree:\n        for n in m.node_tree.nodes:\n            inps = {inp.name: getattr(inp, \"default_value\", None) for inp in n.inputs}\n            clean_inps = {}\n            for k, v in inps.items():\n                if hasattr(v, \"__len__\") and not isinstance(v, str):\n                    clean_inps[k] = tuple(round(float(x), 4) for x in v)\n                elif isinstance(v, (int, float)):\n                    clean_inps[k] = round(float(v), 4)\n            print(f\"  Node {n.name} ({n.type}): {clean_inps}\")\n        if m.node_tree.animation_data:\n            for d in m.node_tree.animation_data.drivers:\n                vars_info = [(v.name, v.type, [(t.id.name if t.id else None, t.data_path) for t in v.targets]) for v in d.driver.variables]\n                print(f\"  Driver {d.data_path}[{d.array_index}] expr={d.driver.expression!r} vars={vars_info}\")\n\nprint(\"\\n=== CHECK LOCAL REST COORDINATES IN v4_stage_rig.blend / v5_stage_env.blend ===\")\nbpy.ops.wm.open_mainfile(filepath=r\"D:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\\LATEST\\v5_stage_env.blend\")\nrig2 = bpy.data.objects[\"RIG_F1_Race\"]\nfor name in (\"GEO_F1_Cockpit_SteeringWheel\", \"GEO_F1_Steering_LCDScreen\", \"GEO_F1_Halo_CenterPylon\",\n             \"GEO_F1_Halo_Hoop\", \"GEO_F1_Overhead_TCam\", \"GEO_F1_Nosecone\", \"GEO_F1_FIA_RainLight\",\n             \"GEO_F1_BrakeGlow_FL\", \"GEO_F1_BrakeDisc_FL\", \"GEO_F1_BrakeCaliper_FL\"):\n    o = bpy.data.objects.get(name)\n    if o:\n        bb = [o.matrix_world @ Vector(c) for c in o.bound_box]\n        mn = tuple(round(min(v[i] for v in bb), 3) for i in range(3))\n        mx = tuple(round(max(v[i] for v in bb), 3) for i in range(3))\n        print(f\"  ENV {name:30s}: parent_type={o.parent_type} parent_bone={o.parent_bone!r} bbox={mn} .. {mx}\")\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\a98b6c71-b658-48ee-9b28-e9a1c116099c\\scratch\\inspect_car_details.py"}}]}
