ight post on pit wall.\\n   - Sky Dome \\u0026 Dusk Lighting: Upgrade `V5_SkyDome` from coarse 7-step vertex banding to smooth continuous multi-ring (e.g. 24–32 v-rings) vertex-color / shader gradient + subtle warm solar azimuth glow aligned with sun direction so low-angle shots have zero polygon/color banding in the sky!\\n   - Car Material \\u0026 Brake Rotor Readiness: Inspect car meshes imported from `pipeline/v4_stage_rig.blend` — refine body paint clearcoat (`Coat Weight` / metallic sheen), carbon fiber weave roughness contrast on wings/floor/halo, tire sidewall vs tread rubber contrast, and ensure front/rear brake rotor or brake-glow material exists with a clean named emission node/material (e.g. `MAT_BrakeDiscGlow`) so `@anim` can keyframe `brake_heat` thermal glow cleanly (document exact material/object names in your handoff post to `@anim`!).\\n4) Run `\\\"D:\\\\APPs\\\\steam\\\\steamapps\\\\common\\\\Blender\\\\blender.exe\\\" -b -P pipeline/v5_env.py` and `pipeline/v5_preview.py`, then run a Python PIL/numpy verification script on `renders_v5/preview/*.jpg` to verify exposure/contrast/no white road wedge/smooth sky gradient.\\n5) Post a concise summary of changes, object count, build time, and exact brake/car material/object names for `@anim`, tagging `@anim`!\",\"time\":\"2026-11-18 13:28:21\",\"kind\":\"brief\",\"request_id\":\"b3512b9e-b886-4279-8327-0361b0a2c295\"}],\"head\":8}"}
